{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>We give thanks</b> — with attached lamed and also without it, it is correct, like the word of זמרה אזמרך ויזמרו לך. And the meaning of 'twice' is to indicate that we give thanks to you time after time, or at every time." "<b>And Your name is near</b> — to answer, for thus our ancestors recounted to us, and he did not mention the recounters, like: אשר ילדה אותה (who bore her). And the correct interpretation is that these recounters are prophets who recounted to us about Your name."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 75, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:34.396737406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}